## The one commit after the merges
commit e9a2f9c15c27cdb88a5d43c0f003ce1c3b7b9740
Author: Usain <usain@immortalcommunicate.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 20 19:23:11 2026 +0100

    Integration 4: map the round-4 residual branch's 19 new tests into the evidence map (IP-R4-WS01-3, R4-IP-2)
    
    `gov contract verify` already returned CONTRACT_SOURCE_BOUND straight after the two merges: the residual branch
    renamed, removed and `#[ignore]`d nothing, so no owner of P2-AR-0042's map became unresolved. What was missing was
    R4-IP-2: the 19 tests the residual runs added (14 certification, 5 lib) owned no capability.
    
    Route, exactly as P2-AR-0042 documents it (its report §11, IP-R4-WS01-3): 36 owner entries added to
    `release/capability-baseline/repair-1/r4-ws01/evidence/mapping/owner-spec.yaml` under a labelled comment (nothing
    existing changed or removed), then its `apply_owner_spec.py`, then `gov contract compile`. The map, the source lock
    and the generated view are the product's own output; none was hand-edited.
    
    The capabilities are the ones the residual reports themselves name (P2-AR-0043 §7 R4-IP-2, P2-AR-0053 §5,
    P2-AR-0055 §9): K3/F4/F3/K2 for the registration and installation tests, W6/O5 for the rebuild-time propagation,
    S6 for the T2 binding status, B1/B2 for the shadowed rule, B1/B3/S5 for the store relocation, D4/D5 for the
    retrieval-profile identity, L4/O5 for the availability handoffs.
    
    `gov contract verify`: CONTRACT_SOURCE_BOUND, 101 capabilities, 798 owners (was 762), 0 deferred, nothing absent
    from the tree. Test owners 441 -> 477. Checklist items naming an owner 586 -> 587. 76 capabilities keep a G-tier
    owner and the same 16 are owned only by tests, so P2-AR-0042's disclosed gaps are unchanged.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

